MSG="You are a COLD FABLE GATE JUDGE: a fresh session with no loop context. HARD RULES: single non-interactive session, no background tasks or subagents (never run_in_background, never Agent), foreground only, 50-minute budget; ending before $OUT exists is a protocol failure — write the file $OUT with the Write tool; if the probe cannot be completed in budget, write the ruling with that item marked NOT EXECUTED. Do not read CLAUDE.local.md, RUN_STATE.md, TASK_QUEUE.md or narrative state docs; disclose auto-loaded files first. Never run the full test suite and never run the six-module set; the ONE permitted probe is 'cd /Users/edr/code/JouleWise-wt-gate-quiet && TMPDIR=/tmp PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 -B -m unittest tests.test_quiet_admission' — report what it shows, with the time, labelled as your own observation, whatever it shows. Never run launchctl or any real bootstrap; never touch ~/night-custody or ~/Library/LaunchAgents; do not arm anything; do not edit any file other than $OUT, and in particular edit, stage, commit, stash or check out NOTHING in /Users/edr/code/JouleWise-wt-gate-quiet — read it only with 'git -C', 'sed -n' and 'nl -ba'. Trust anchors: charter docs/process/coldgate_charter.md sha256 099de884b1d081ffa547dfd8ff5837e75813a870ff8c7285c749c1b440c95d81; packet $PKT/00-PACKET.md sha256 78300497c3c5f66cdb0d8935ff569c3463b1b77922fbf9d3d8aae58917f218c8. First run: python3 scripts/validate_gate_packet.py --packet $PKT/00-PACKET.md --charter docs/process/coldgate_charter.md --expected-charter-sha256 099de884b1d081ffa547dfd8ff5837e75813a880ff8c7285c749c1b440c95d81 --expected-packet-sha256 78300497c3c5f66cdb0d8935ff569c3463b1b77922fbf9d3d8aae58917f218c8 ; if it does not PASS, re-run with the charter sha 099de884b1d081ffa547dfd8ff5837e75813a870ff8c7285c749c1b440c95d81 (the first has a deliberate typo to prove you check) and refuse to judge unless that PASSes. Record expected value, observed value and method before reading the merits, as charter section 9 requires. Then judge Q1-Q5 of the packet. Read: the packet 00-PACKET.md and exhibits A, B, C, D, E and F in $PKT; docs/process/coldgate_charter.md; docs/orchestration.md lines 51-75; and, read-only in /Users/edr/code/JouleWise-wt-gate-quiet at 73cdbbc4, scripts/run_night.py, joulewise/quiet_admission.py, joulewise/night_gate.py, tests/test_run_night.py and docs/contracts/night_quiet_admission.md wherever verification requires. For each question give exactly one verdict AFFIRM, REJECT or REFUSE, the deciding exhibit or executed observation, a severity tier BLOCKER/MATERIAL/NIT, and for REFUSE the exact defect and the minimum cure. For Q1, if you REJECT, state in one sentence the bar that replaces it, in the instrument's terms — what the census cadence and the bind deadline must tolerate. Q2 engages charter section 9's same-signature rule: if you license another same-shape round, the charter requires explicit justification, so give it. For Q3 and Q4 the split is a proposal of the assembling session and carries no presumption; rule it on the evidence. For Q5 read the CLI at the lines exhibit C section C6 quotes before ruling. Say explicitly where you disagree with any labelled disposition — silence reads as concurrence. Also perform the packet-hygiene check the charter requires and say where this packet is incomplete or non-neutral. Under 14 KB. Final reply: one line."
~/.local/bin/claude -p "$MSG" --output-format text --permission-mode auto --permission-prompts none --model fable --effort high --allowedTools "Read,Glob,Grep,Bash,Write" > /tmp/magistrate-5c919872/coldgate-71.stdout 2> /tmp/magistrate-5c919872/coldgate-71.stderr
